    </p>
    <p>
      These Terms cover only the hosted part: the RAS Connect relay, the accounts it holds, the
      credentials it issues, the managed endpoints it provisions, and the notifications it delivers.
      Running RAS Code on your own machines, or running your own copy of the relay from the source,
      is outside their scope.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="accounts">
    <p class="section-number">03</p>
    <h2>Accounts</h2>
    <p>
      RAS Connect requires an account, provided through Clerk. Keep your credentials secure, and get
      in touch promptly if you think your account has been used without your permission. You are
      responsible for what happens through your account and through the devices and environments you
      link to it.
    </p>
    <p>
      One account is for one person. Do not share credentials, impersonate someone else, or create
      accounts by automated means.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="personal-use">
    <p class="section-number">04</p>
    <h2>Personal Use Only</h2>
    <p>
      RAS Connect is offered for your own personal or internal use, at no charge, and with no service
      commitment. You may not:
    </p>
    <ul>
